7141229487,"node_id":"LE_lADOAGuhRc5PJn9jzwAAAAGppoOv","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python/mypy/issues/events/7141229487","actor":{"login":"AlexWaygood","id":66076021,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2MDc2MDIx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/66076021?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlexWaygood","html_url":"https://github.com/AlexWaygood","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlexWaygood/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlexWaygood/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlexWaygood/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlexWaygood/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlexWaygood/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlexWaygood/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlexWaygood/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlexWaygood/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlexWaygood/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"event":"labeled","commit_id":null,"commit_url":null,"created_at":"2022-08-06T17:54:40Z","label":{"name":"topic-type-alias","color":"51FABE"},"performed_via_github_app":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python/mypy/issues/comments/2453214310","html_url":"https://github.com/python/mypy/issues/13320#issuecomment-2453214310","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python/mypy/issues/13320","id":2453214310,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAGuhRc6SORRm","user":{"login":"brianschubert","id":25313350,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1MzEzMzUw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/25313350?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brianschubert","html_url":"https://github.com/brianschubert","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brianschubert/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brianschubert/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brianschubert/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brianschubert/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brianschubert/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brianschubert/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brianschubert/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brianschubert/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brianschubert/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-02T22:37:02Z","updated_at":"2024-11-02T22:37:02Z","body":"The reason this doesn't work is becaused calls to `builtins.dict` get translsated into `DictExpr`s  during semantic analysis ([here](https://github.com/python/mypy/blob/1f200dde451493a070b9464011998dd837df4bc2/mypy/semanal.py#L5768-L5769)), which causes the usual call expression analysis to be skipped during type checking ([here](https://github.com/python/mypy/blob/1f200dde451493a070b9464011998dd837df4bc2/mypy/checkexpr.py#L476)). The fix to make this work would be trivial (we'd just need to add a check for `isinstance(node, DictExpr)` to [this branch](https://github.com/python/mypy/blob/1f200dde451493a070b9464011998dd837df4bc2/mypy/checkexpr.py#L477) so that the call expression gets analyzed even though the result isn't used). However, I'm not sure that that would be worth doing, since using type aliases for their runtime values is already a bit dubious. The \"correct\" way to write this would be\r\n```python\r\na: Values = dict(foo=\"\")\r\n```\r\nwhich has the helpful error\r\n```none\r\nerror: Dict entry 0 has incompatible type \"str\": \"str\"; expected \"str\": \"int\"\r\n```\r\nBy comparison, fixing this would result in the less helpful error\r\n```\r\nerror: No overload variant of \"dict\" matches argument type \"str\"\r\nnote:     def dict(self) -> dict[str, int]\r\nnote:     def dict(self, **kwargs: int) -> dict[str, int]\r\nnote:     def dict(self, SupportsKeysAndGetItem[str, int], /) -> dict[str, int]\r\nnote:     def dict(self, SupportsKeysAndGetItem[str, int], /, **kwargs: int) -> dict[str, int]\r\nnote:     def dict(self, Iterable[tuple[str, int]], /) -> dict[str, int]\r\nnote:     def dict(self, Iterable[tuple[str, int]], /, **kwargs: int) -> dict[str, int]\r\nnote:     def dict(self, Iterable[list[str]], /) -> dict[str, str]\r\nnote:     def dict(self, Iterable[list[bytes]], /) -> dict[bytes, bytes]\r\n```","author_association":"COLLABORATOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python/mypy/issues/comments/2453214310/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"brianschubert","id":25313350,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1MzEzMzUw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/25313350?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brianschubert","html_url":"https://github.com/brianschubert","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brianschubert/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brianschubert/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brianschubert/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brianschubert/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brianschubert/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brianschubert/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brianschubert/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brianschubert/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brianschubert/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"actor":{"login":"hauntsaninja","id":12621235,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyNjIxMjM1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12621235?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hauntsaninja","html_u